# =============================================================================
# BUILD 01 (WORKING): NEXUS Multi-Collection Financial Exchange & Risk Engine
# =============================================================================
# All 5 collections (Traders, Assets, Orders, Positions, Audits) compiled into
# a single native binary via LLVM IR.
#
# Fixes applied where our first attempt was wrong:
#   1. Use "using order_id" instead of "by order_id" after "order" so the
#      2-word lexicon phrase "order by" (SORTBY) does not swallow "order".
#   2. Name the collection in duplicate policies ("If an order already exists,
#      reject it.") once more than one collection exists in the file.
#   3. Name foreign-key fields "buyer_or_seller" / "holder" instead of "trader"
#      so FIELD normalization does not shadow the Traders collection.
#   4. Express liquidation and fee math using fixed-point basis points (/ 10000)
#      instead of dividing by a runtime variable.
# =============================================================================

# ---- 1. Collections & Schema ------------------------------------------------

Traders is a collection.
Each trader has a handle (text), cash_cents (number), margin_limit (number), realized_pnl (number), risk_score (number), tier (number) and frozen (number).
No two traders share the same handle.
If a trader already exists, reject it.

Assets is a collection.
Each asset has a ticker (text), mark_price (number), prev_close (number), volatility_bps (number), volume (number), high_watermark (number) and halted (number).
No two assets share the same ticker.
If an asset already exists, replace it.

Orders is a collection.
Each order has an order_id (number), a buyer_or_seller (text), a symbol (text), a side (number), a limit_price (number), a qty (number), a notional (number), a priority_rank (number) and a status (number).
No two orders share the same order_id.
If an order already exists, reject it.

Positions is a collection.
Each position has a pos_key (text), a holder (text), an asset_sym (text), units (number), entry_price (number), current_price (number), unrealized_pnl (number), leverage_bps (number), margin_used (number) and liquidated (number).
No two positions share the same pos_key.
If a position already exists, replace it.

Audits is a collection.
Each audit has a seq_no (number), a category (text), an actor (text), a delta_cents (number), a severity (number) and an epoch (number).
No two audits share the same seq_no.
If an audit already exists, reject it.
Keep audits in the order they were added.

# ---- 2. Taught Domain Vocabulary --------------------------------------------

"solvent" means frozen is 0 and risk_score under 8000.
"overleveraged" means risk_score at least 8000.
"underwater" means unrealized_pnl under 0.
"in the money" means unrealized_pnl over 0.
"whale" means cash_cents at least 100000000.

An active trader is a trader whose frozen is 0.
A vip trader is an active trader whose tier is at least 3.
A risky trader is an active trader overleveraged.

An open order is an order whose status is 1.
A bid order is an open order whose side is 1.
An ask order is an open order whose side is -1.

An open position is a position whose liquidated is 0.
A profitable position is an open position in the money.
A losing position is an open position underwater.

A critical audit is an audit whose severity is at least 3.

# ---- 3. Trader Capabilities -------------------------------------------------

register-trader: add a trader.
lookup-trader: find a trader by handle.
drop-trader: remove a trader by handle.

deposit-cash: increase cash_cents by a given amount for traders whose handle is a given handle.
withdraw-cash: decrease cash_cents by a given amount for traders whose handle is a given handle.
book-pnl: for every trader whose handle is a given handle, increase cash_cents by a given delta, then increase realized_pnl by a given delta.
recompute-trader-risk: for every active trader, set risk_score to (risk_score * 90) / 100 + 50.
freeze-risky-traders: for every risky trader, set frozen to 1.
unfreeze-trader: set frozen to 0 for traders whose handle is a given handle.
promote-whales: for every active trader whale, increase tier by 1 and increase margin_limit by 25 percent.

top-traders: show the top 5 traders by cash_cents.
whales: show the handle, cash_cents and tier of active traders whale sorted by cash_cents descending.
frozen-traders: show the handle and risk_score of traders whose frozen is 1.
total-exchange-cash: what is the total cash_cents of traders?
average-trader-risk: what is the average risk_score of active traders?
active-trader-count: how many active traders are there?

# ---- 4. Asset & Market Feed Capabilities ------------------------------------

upsert-asset: add an asset.
quote-asset: find an asset by ticker.
delist-asset: remove an asset by ticker.

# Sequential in-place update: updates mark_price, volume, and volatility_bps in one fused pass
tick-asset-price: for every asset whose ticker is a given ticker and halted is 0, set mark_price to a given new_price, then increase volume by a given trade_qty, then set volatility_bps to (volatility_bps * 80) / 100 + 20.
update-high-watermarks: for every asset whose mark_price is over high_watermark, set high_watermark to mark_price.
trigger-circuit-breakers: for every asset whose volatility_bps is at least 5000, set halted to 1.
reset-circuit-breakers: for every asset whose halted is 1, set halted to 0 and halve volatility_bps.
market-crash-shock: for every asset whose halted is 0, decrease mark_price by 15 percent and increase volatility_bps by 1500.

most-volatile-assets: show the top 5 assets by volatility_bps.
halted-assets: show the ticker, mark_price and volatility_bps of assets whose halted is 1.
total-market-volume: what is the total volume of assets?

# ---- 5. Order Book Capabilities ---------------------------------------------

submit-order: add an order.
# Note: "using" instead of "by" avoids the 2-word lexicon phrase "order by" (SORTBY)
inspect-order: find an order using order_id.
cancel-order: remove an order using order_id.

# Sequential assignment computes notional = limit_price * qty and priority_rank in place
stamp-order-metrics: for every open order, set notional to limit_price * qty, then set priority_rank to limit_price * side * 1000 + qty.
mark-order-filled: for every open order whose order_id is a given order_id, set status to 2 and set qty to 0.
cancel-trader-orders: remove orders whose buyer_or_seller is a given buyer_or_seller and status is 1.
purge-closed-orders: keep orders whose status is 1.

best-bids: show the top 5 bid orders by limit_price.
best-asks: show the bottom 5 ask orders by limit_price.
symbol-bids: show the order_id, buyer_or_seller, limit_price and qty of bid orders whose symbol is a given symbol sorted by limit_price descending.
symbol-asks: show the order_id, buyer_or_seller, limit_price and qty of ask orders whose symbol is a given symbol sorted by limit_price ascending.
largest-open-orders: show the top 5 open orders by notional.
open-bid-volume: what is the total qty of bid orders?
open-ask-volume: what is the total qty of ask orders?
open-order-count: how many open orders are there?

# ---- 6. Position & Margin Risk Capabilities ---------------------------------

open-position: add a position.
inspect-position: find a position by pos_key.
close-position: remove a position by pos_key.

# Multi-step sequential mark-to-market valuation and basis-points margin calculation in one pass
mark-to-market: for every open position whose asset_sym is a given asset_sym, set current_price to a given new_mark, then set unrealized_pnl to units * (current_price - entry_price), then set margin_used to (units * current_price * leverage_bps) / 10000.

apply-funding-rate: for every open position, decrease unrealized_pnl by (margin_used * 5) / 1000.
liquidate-insolvent: for every losing position whose unrealized_pnl is under -500000, set liquidated to 1 and set units to 0 and set margin_used to 0.

biggest-winners: show the top 5 profitable positions by unrealized_pnl.
biggest-losers: show the bottom 5 losing positions by unrealized_pnl.
liquidated-positions: show the pos_key, holder, asset_sym and unrealized_pnl of positions whose liquidated is 1.
total-unrealized-pnl: what is the total unrealized_pnl of open positions?
total-margin-used: what is the total margin_used of open positions?
worst-drawdown: what is the lowest unrealized_pnl of open positions?

# ---- 7. Ordered Compliance Audit Log Capabilities ---------------------------

log-audit: add an audit.
find-audit: find an audit by seq_no.
redact-audit: remove an audit by seq_no.

recent-first-audits: show the first 5 audits.
critical-audits: show the seq_no, category, actor and delta_cents of critical audits.
audit-count: how many audits are there?

# ---- 8. Pure Arithmetic Pricer & Fee Calculators ----------------------------

calc-taker-fee: take notional_cents and fee_bps and return (notional_cents * fee_bps) / 10000.
calc-2x-liq-price: take entry_cents and return entry_cents - entry_cents / 2.
calc-5x-liq-price: take entry_cents and return entry_cents - entry_cents / 5.
calc-10x-liq-price: take entry_cents and return entry_cents - entry_cents / 10.
